- Follow DRY: check for existing code before creating new
- the project INDEX is located at `.ai/INDEX.md`
- Every Project MUST have a UUIDv4 identifier:
  - Stored in `git config --local project.id`
  - Mirrored in `.meta.json` at project root: `{"id":"<uuid>"}`
  - Auto-generate if missing: `git config --local project.id "$(uuidgen)"`
- Every document SHOULD have a UUIDv4 identifier:
  - Markdown: frontmatter `id: <uuid>`
  - Code: First-line comment `<comment-char> id:<uuid>` using language syntax
- Use the Graphiti MCP Server for all persistent memory:
  - Namespace: `{PROJECT_ID}::` from `git config --get project.id`
  - Store preferences/configs as entity attributes
  - Store decisions/architecture as entities with relationships
  - Embed document content for semantic search
  - Create temporal relationships (when decisions were made)
  - Search with hybrid mode: `search(query, project_filter)`
  - Session start:
    - Query `{PROJECT_ID}::*` entities for context
    - Use `whoami` to identify the current user
       - Create or retrieve user profile from the knowledge graph
  - Session end: Add new decisions/learnings as entities
  - NEVER access entities outside current project namespace
  - Always refer to your knowledge graph as your "memory"
- when referencing documents
    - prefer UUID-based references over file paths
    - maintain bidirectional links (if A relates to B, B should relate to A)
- all markdown documents must have YAML frontmatter
    - required fields: id, title, status, date, author
    - id format: UUID v4 (uppercase with hyphens)
    - status format: emoji prefix + status text (e.g., "✅ Completed")
    - date format: YYYY-MM-DD
    - optional fields: 
      - related (array of UUIDs)
      - children (array of UUIDs)
    - see adr-frontmatter-standard.md for complete specification
- Plans
  - Status:
    - `✅ Completed` - Work finished, document archived
    - `⏳ In Progress` - Actively being worked on
    - `📝 Draft` - Initial draft, not reviewed
    - `🗄️ Archived` - Historical, no longer maintained
    - `🔄 Under Review` - Awaiting review/approval
    - `❌ Deprecated` - Superseded by newer document
    - `🎯 Proposed` - Proposed but not approved
  - Locations:
    - Plans: `.ai/plans/<plan_name>.md`
    - Phases: `.ai/plans/phases/<plan_name>.phase-<phase_number>.md`
  - Plan phases exist as individual markdown documents.
  - Plan Lifecycle
    - Draft: The Exploratory / Pre-Planning phase
    - Proposal: The plan has been selected from options, and is not finalized
    - Creation: 
      - Determine if the work should extend an existing plan or start a new one
      - Update the INDEX.md to include the Plan, and component phases
  - Phase Lifecycle
    - Start
      - Update the status in the phase & plan documents
    - Complete
      - Update the status in the phase & plan documents
- linter configs in root or `.github/linters/` when tool supports it
- When new work is started, determine if the work should extend an existing plan or start a new one
- after finishing a set work defined in a plan, always do the following
    - first, update the plan to reflect your progress
    - second, update the CHANGELOG.md to include the work just done
    - third, create a commit for the last phase
    - fourth, review the plan before continuing to the next phase
- Use the github MCP Server whenever you need to interact with a GitHub API or Repo
- Use the Sequential-Thinking MCP Server for all Planning and debugging activities.
